Subject: [PATCH] Data Exchange, STEP - Progress of related and mapped
 representations

STEPControl_ActorRead gave the shape of a product a scope of two steps, one
for its own representation and one for the representations related to it,
but TransferRelatedSRR took a step of that scope for each relationship. With
two or more relationships, every representation after the first was
translated with an empty range: no progress, and UserBreak() never asked.
A hybrid model as CATIA V6 writes it, solids and curves in two related
representations, translated its solids for 11 s without either.

The mapped item path opened a scope on its range and then passed the same
range on to the mapped representation, which Message_ProgressScope asserts
against in debug builds; the representation's translation reported nothing.

TransferRelatedSRR takes a range and gives each relationship a share of it;
the mapped representation and the representations related to it each get a
step of the mapped item's scope.
